, as well as commercial and industrial loans. In addition, the company provides insurance brokerage services, such as individual and business insurance policies; holds and markets real estate properties; and debit and credit cards, as well as acts as the trustee. Further, it offers technology and data services; and personalized financial guidance and investment services. It serves consumers; small, mid-sized and large businesses; and owners and developers of commercial real estate. The company was formerly known as Washington Federal, Inc. and changed its name to WaFd, Inc. in September 2023. WaFd, Inc. was founded in 1917 and is headquartered in Seattle, Washington.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brent J. Beardall CPA | President, CEO & Vice Chairman | Age 54 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $405K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $105K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["WaFd, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $2.0B market cap on $815M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 9% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $212M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 26 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.96\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 11.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 57% margin 